Save93 / Whiterun exterior / DynDOLOD continuation / 2026-11-09

Runtime and procedure
- Skyrim AE 1.6.1170.0, SSE Display Tweaks 0.5.16, 42 FPS game cap and dynamic Papyrus budget enabled, 60 FPS loading screen cap.
- Save93 loaded once per launch. Each trial entered Bannered Mare (0001605E), waited for steady interior cadence, and returned to WhiterunWorld (0001A27F). Four measured exterior returns in ABBA order. The real DynDOLOD and other load-order mods supplied the workload. Later trials inherit in-session state.
- Off and on shared tracing. The continuation was armed only after confirming arrival and the loading menu had closed. 32 Utility.Wait(0.01) responses per trial from about one second after arrival, with one pending SKSE task.
- Total measures the time from the exterior request to completion of the last tracked cell event. Drain starts at confirmed arrival. The event cohort consists of cell roots queued from request until probe start. Tail wait sums root Q->P and native Q->P on the last completed root. It includes loading and excludes separately timed native execution.
- Frame intervals are PresentMon QPC gaps validated against engine render counts. Steady windows use the last two seconds. Post-load frame metrics cover the probe window.
- Save93 original files checked before and after. SHA256 ESS 87C181889BB60A565C327FF0AA0B1B6F46D568AC0EB29C022925A3912742277D
- SHA256 SKSE 5EE67E98B488FAE5BD5C1E5A9A87DA9D92522D480255F2F1BA84E6FB80F1B0AA
- Final APBGameplayTrace.dll SHA256 565AA7B3F67850A08AC2BD252D9120C822A84608846433CA7A192F23F8FEE458
- Test DLL and copied profile archived after completion. MO2 profile restored to TKL - MUNG ADDON - SPS Test.

Final implementation and observations
- Stock drain/retry use the original SSE Display Tweaks budget. After a stock function call returns, the test admits only the just-returned DynDOLOD root at the front of the existing tasklet queue, with a stock native byte and identity check and a same-render-frame deadline. Stock target-object locking and VM result marshalling stay in the engine path.
- Scope is at most one resumed tasklet and one newly eligible stock getter per render frame. The 0.25 ms check is an admission deadline. Processing time is checked after the engine routine returns, and a slice exceeding 0.5 ms disables further attempts in that trial.
- Four eligible off candidates, one on continuation in two on trials. The successful continuation occurred on the last tracked stack in trial 3. Its engine tasklet took 0.0201 ms including the check and continuation.
- For stack 1488833, thread 30496, render frame 9113, stock FormList.GetAt return -> inline ObjectReference.GetWorldSpace dispatch took 0.0117 ms. Enqueue -> tasklet acceptance was 0.0017 ms. Both native dispatches and returns are present on the same thread. The render sampler measured a local 22.075 ms interval. This was in the 42 FPS-capped run, with some transition frames faster than the cap and exactly 84 frames in each final two-second window.
- Trial 3 stock GetAt before the promotion held the list lock for 23.4145 ms from G to X. The promoted GetWorldSpace reused the reacquired root lock, then the original VM switched targets and acquired the list lock for the next GetAt. No GetAt itself was promoted. After the promoted getter, the next GetAt queued and completed via stock processing. Its Q->P was 0.0686 ms.
- For context, on the same DynDOLOD root type after arrival, 56 off GetAt return -> next GetWorldSpace dispatch samples had trial medians of about 23.3 ms and 18.6 ms. These include natural queue and locking differences across different instances and are not paired counterfactuals.
- Response p95 after excluding the first four probes from each trial as a sensitivity check was off 39.844 ms and on 39.575 ms. One on trial never activated and the largest off spikes clustered near the start of a trial. Attribution of aggregate gains or regressions to the single continuation is unsupported.
- Stock locking is tied to VM stack ownership. AE 1.6.1170 disassembly at Address Library IDs 104257 and 104258 shows a successful new acquisition incrementing the owning stack reference count, then release decrementing it. The lock can span the handoff to the native queue. This supports preserving the engine acquisition/release path. Earlier scheduling can still change ordering against other scripts, array observations and object binding timing. This short run proves a successful dispatch/return, not general lifetime safety or equivalence of returned object identity under concurrent mutation.
- Earlier in this session, an indoor-window pilot was invalid because rendering did not stabilize during capture. The staged phase-end ABBA below completed but never activated the extra execution. Its on/off variation demonstrates how the last completing root and measured wait can change without intervention.

Verification
- xmake build APBGameplayTrace and xmake build AdaptivePapyrusBudget succeeded. xmake run budget_policy_tests passed.
- Trace analyzer accepted a synthetic same-stack/thread/frame continuation and rejected wrong thread, stack and frame records.
- Both staged and final runs produced four complete captures, with no dropped trace events. PresentMon warned about process-query privileges. The captured Skyrim frame counts agreed with the independent render counter in the measured windows.
- Raw folders: build/gameplay-trace/cell-42-continuation-budget-ab and build/gameplay-trace/cell-42-continuation-staged-ab.
- f is a stock matching return. m is a queue guard rejection. H is an eligible disabled candidate. h is a resumed tasklet, i a scoped immediate getter, k completion of the slice.

